Subject: [PATCH] Allocate pmem-ext2 below the ARM64 linear mapping limit

Top-down allocation can place the store above PHYSMEM_END, causing
nd_pmem to reject it with EINVAL. Allocate from the bottom as the regular
PMEM device already does.

--- a/src/crosvm/sys/linux/device_helpers.rs
+++ b/src/crosvm/sys/linux/device_helpers.rs
@@ -1357,7 +1357,9 @@
                 Alloc::PmemDevice(index),
                 format!("pmem_ext2_image_{index}"),
                 AllocOptions::new()
-                .top_down(true)
+                // Keep the store within the guest kernel's linear mapping range,
+                // as with regular PMEM devices.
+                .top_down(false)
                 .prefetchable(true)
                 // 2MB alignment for DAX
                 // cf. https://docs.pmem.io/persistent-memory/getting-started-guide/creating-development-environments/linux-environments/advanced-topics/i-o-alignment-considerations#verifying-io-alignment
